[[File:Trader Temmie (Beta 6.7).png|thumb|208x208px|Beta 6.7]]
Trader Temmie was one of the 20 new cards released in '''Beta 6.6''' as an excelent card: A 4/6 monster with the ability of adding a random spell of your soul to your hand at the end of your turn. For only 5G. This was quickly noticed to be overpowered, so in the very next update, '''Beta 6.7''', its ATK got nerfed from 4 to 3. '''Beta 7.1''' nerfed it further by making its effect trigger at the start of your turn instead of at the end. '''Beta 32.0''' buffed it a bit by reducing the cost of given spells by 1, similar to [[Echo Flower]].
[[File:Trader Temmie (Beta 7.1).png|thumb|212x212px|Beta 7.1]]
It stayed like this until '''Beta 55.0''', in which its effect was changed to trigger at the end of every turn again and no longer give the cost reduction. But instead of any spell of your soul, it adds a 0-1G spell of any soul. It also gained Transparency and its stats were changed to 4/4/4, effectively gaining +1/-2 and -1 cost. ([[Bratty]] took its old design until Beta 56.0.)
[[File:Trader Temmie (Beta 32.0).png|thumb|212x212px|Beta 32.0]]

